# Throwaway test fixtures — invented names, seeded accounts with known passwords.
# Useful locally, not something the repo should carry.
Resouces/CSV/dummyData/

# Real roster data — these carry the actual squad's names, and most of the
# players are minors. The blank templates beside them are tracked on purpose;
# what is excluded here is the filled-in kind. Note FR-SO-BHS_Player_Template
# is named like a template but holds a real Fr/So roster, which is exactly why
# it is listed by name rather than trusting the naming convention.
Resouces/CSV/Jr Varsity.xlsx
Resouces/CSV/Recording Numbers.xlsx
Resouces/CSV/FR-SO-BHS_Player_Template.xlsx
Resouces/CSV/varsity_roster_export.csv
Resouces/CSV/*_roster_export.csv

# Local reference material and scratch assets — source documents for the daily
# thoughts and quiz content, ad-hoc account-admin notes, and a stray image.
# The app reads none of them; the content that ships lives in Postgres.
#
# The account-admin files are working notes rather than runnable SQL, and they
# name real people by email address. That is the reason they stay out: git
# history is permanent, and a repo is a poor place to keep a coach's address.
#
# pubschls.xlsx is the California Department of Education's public school
# directory (https://www.cde.ca.gov/ds/si/ds/pubschls.asp) — ~9 MB of third-
# party data, re-downloadable in one request, and stale the moment it lands.
# It was the source for the away-venue addresses, and those are already
# captured where they matter: in the database, and in the script under
# Resouces/SQL/ that put them there. Carrying the whole directory in git
# would add a large binary that nothing reads.
Resouces/Thoughts4TheDay/
Resouces/CSV/pubschls.xlsx
Resouces/SQL/resetPassword.sql
Resouces/SQL/removeUser.sql
assets/soccerPlayer.png
deployed.bat
